Mozilla-derived public CA certificates

This package preserves curl's 2026-09-25 PEM conversion of Mozilla's public
CA certificate data without changes. The complete upstream header and all
certificate labels remain in cacert.pem. The bundle is governed by the Mozilla
Public License, Version 2.0; a copy is included as LICENSE.

Upstream PEM and corresponding source information:
https://curl.se/ca/cacert-2026-09-25.pem
https://curl.se/docs/caextract.html
https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mozilla-firefox/firefox/refs/heads/release/security/nss/lib/ckfw/builtins/certdata.txt

The dated PEM snapshot and its SHA-256 checksum identify the distributed data.
share/ca-certificates/source.txt records conversion details and the source-data
SHA-256 from the upstream PEM header. The Mozilla source URL names an upstream
branch for provenance; it is not consulted during a Pyxis build.

curl documents that this PEM conversion omits Mozilla's additional trust-store
constraints. It is not the complete browser trust policy. Pyxis performs no
boot-time download or automatic trust update; updating the recipe requires
reviewing a new dated snapshot, rebuilding the image and restarting providers.

